; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Rhyming Poem Machine
; CATEGORY: Stories, Chatbots & Language
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     poetry, rhyme, random, lists of lists
; SUMMARY:  Writes a four-line rhyming poem from families of rhyming words, then displays it on a starry night sky.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Words are kept in rhyme families, such as [night light kite
;   flight]. Each couplet picks one family and uses two different words
;   from it to end two lines, so the lines rhyme. Line starters are
;   picked from another list so each poem is fresh. The poem is shown
;   in the turtle world under a sky full of stars.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run for a new poem. Add a new rhyme family to RHYMES and new
;   line starters to OPENERS to change the poems.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a list of lists: each inner list is a rhyme family
;   * picking two different items: pick one, REMOVE it, pick again
;   * AABB rhyme scheme: lines 1 and 2 rhyme, lines 3 and 4 rhyme
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Change the scheme to ABAB
;   * Add a title made from one of the rhyming words
; ============================================================

make "rhymes [[night light kite flight] [moon spoon balloon tune] [sea tree bee key] [sky pie butterfly] [day bay hay play] [rain train lane plane]]
make "openers [[The cat sat watching the] [I looked up into the] [We ran together through the] [A bird was singing of the] [My heart is full of] [Nobody ever saw the] [Under a blanket of] [I dreamed I sailed across the]]

to two.different :family
  localmake "a pick :family
  output list :a pick remove :a :family
end

; Use each opener only once per poem.
to next.opener
  localmake "o pick :openers.left
  make "openers.left remove :o :openers.left
  output :o
end

to couplet
  localmake "pair two.different pick :rhymes
  output list (sentence next.opener first :pair) (sentence next.opener last :pair)
end

to night.sky :lines
  clearscreen hideturtle setbackground [15 20 60]
  repeat 60 [
    penup setxy (random 780) - 390 (random 280) + 10
    setpencolor pick [7 6 [200 200 255]] pendown dot pos
  ]
  ; a crescent moon: a yellow circle, then a sky-colored one over it
  penup setxy 300 200 setpencolor 6 pendown filled 6 [arc 360 40]
  penup setxy 318 212 setpencolor [15 20 60] pendown filled [15 20 60] [arc 360 36]
  setpencolor 7 setlabelheight 22
  localmake "y -20
  foreach :lines [penup setxy -300 :y label ? make "y :y - 50]
end

make "openers.left :openers
make "poem sentence couplet couplet
foreach :poem [print ?]
night.sky :poem
